From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: def_font_scale 115% for the 320 dpi panel

Read by the SettingsProvider patch via loadFractionSetting. 320 dpi buys 540 dp of width, which is
what dense layouts need, at the cost of physically small text on 5.2 inches; 1.15 is the second step
of the SettingsLib ladder so it stays a normal, movable selection in Settings.
---
 .../base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
index d2605f5..b790737 100644
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
@@ -19,4 +19,11 @@
 <resources>
     <!-- Set the automatic brightness mode on by default -->
     <bool name="def_screen_brightness_automatic_mode">true</bool>
+
+    <!-- Text one notch up, to compensate for shipping the panel at 320 dpi. That reports this
+         1080x1920 screen as 540 dp wide, which is the room dense layouts need but leaves text
+         physically small on 5.2 inches. 1.15 is the second step of the SettingsLib ladder
+         (0.85 / 1.0 / 1.15 / 1.30), so Settings shows it as a normal selection the user can move
+         either way. Read by DatabaseHelper.loadSystemSettings via loadFractionSetting with base 1. -->
+    <fraction name="def_font_scale">115%</fraction>
 </resources>
